From d022e4e56c0369ff75f75b0762e47396bca18e04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:33:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] S922X: linux: dts: odroid-go-ultra: read the time from
 the RK818 RTC

The RK817 RTC was rtc0, so the system time was read from it at boot.
It seems to run without a 32 kHz crystal: it gained about 1.5% while the
device was on and lost about 14-17% while it was off (about 74 minutes
in 8.6 hours). The RK818 RTC keeps the correct time while the device is
off.

Give each RTC an alias, so that the RK818 RTC always becomes rtc0. The
RTC core looks up the alias of the parent device (the PMIC) when the RTC
device has no DT node of its own. Without an alias, the RK817 RTC would
take rtc0, because it is registered first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts  | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
index cebedab5787f..ea477c366ff9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra.dts
@@ -789,3 +789,20 @@ mipi_out_panel: endpoint {
 		remote-endpoint = <&mipi_in_panel>;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * Lakka: The RK817 RTC seems to run without a 32 kHz crystal on this board
+ * and loses minutes per hour while the device is off, but the RK818 RTC
+ * keeps the correct time. Make the RK818 RTC rtc0, so that the system time
+ * is read from it at boot.
+ *
+ * Give every RTC an alias: an RTC without one takes the lowest free number,
+ * and the RK817 RTC is registered first, so it would take rtc0.
+ */
+/ {
+       aliases {
+               rtc0 = &rk818;
+               rtc1 = &vrtc;
+               rtc2 = &rk817;
+       };
+};
